# Monitoring, Metrics, and Logging

## Metrics Collection
- Use Prometheus for metrics collection, expose metrics on `/metrics` endpoint
- Track: block height/time, TPS, validator performance, network health
- Module-specific: ident verifications, lizenz activations, ANT trading volume, LZN burn rate
- Consensus metrics: block creation time, validator selection

## Logging
- Use structured logging format, include context in all logs (module name, operation, account address, tx hash, block height)
- Implement log rotation, centralize logs for analysis (ELK, Loki, etc.)
- Recover from panics in critical paths, log before recovery
- Mask sensitive information in logs (private keys, passwords)

## Health Checks & Alerting
- Implement `/health` endpoint (check DB, module state, validator status)
- Set up alerts for critical metrics (error rate spikes, performance degradation, validator issues)
- Configure alert channels and set appropriate thresholds
